      "id": "co26-m-frprd-7a",
      "number": "7A",
      "title": "Front Range Passenger Rail District tax and debt",
      "level": "district",
      "type": "measure",
      "description": "Would create a 0.333% sales and use tax ($295 million a year) and authorize $580 million of debt (up to $785 million repayment) to build and run Colorado Connector (CoCo) passenger rail from Pueblo to Fort Collins. Fort Collins is inside the district.",
